# K01 witness (steps/k01-selector-identity-20261001.md §6): the candidate's unused
# incompatible first field must not reject a Consumer that only reads the LAST x --
# admission is by the Consumer's used edges.  The candidate's last x is a size_t like the
# requirement's, so bare `v\x` = 30 is legal; nothing reads occurrence 0.  Success is 7.
Pair: (size_t: x 10U; size_t: x 20U)
Tri: (int: x 7; size_t: x 20U; size_t: x 30U)
fn: lastOnly (Pair: v) int
    size_t: got
    got: v\x
    return: (cast: (int) (got))
end: lastOnly
Tri: t
int: ok 7
if: lastOnly(t) != 30
    ok: 81
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
